{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% from "_macros.html.j2" import source_list %}
{% macro law(section, page) -%}
<a class="rt-cite-link" href="{{ cfg.statute_url }}" title="SB 63 (Stats. 2025, Ch. 740), PDF page {{ page }}">§{{ section }}</a>
{%- endmacro %}
{% block title %}Oversight · {{ cfg.site_title }}{% endblock %}
{% block description %}Who sits on SB 63's Independent Oversight Committee, what it can and cannot require of BART, Muni, AC Transit, and Caltrain, and every recommendation an agency rejects.{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
{% set n_voting = committee.voting | length %}
{% set n_board = committee.by_seat["operator_board"] | length %}
{% set n_expert = committee.by_seat["expert"] | length %}
{% set n_chair = committee.by_seat["mtc_chair"] | length %}
<span class="rt-eyebrow">Who checks the agencies</span>
<h1>Oversight: who reviews the agencies, and what can be enforced</h1>
<p class="rt-lede">SB 63 puts the efficiency review under an oversight committee that includes board members of the
  agencies being reviewed, and leaves enforcement to MTC. This page shows who is on the committee, what it has
  done, what it can and cannot require, and every recommendation an agency formally rejects.</p>

<nav aria-label="On this page" class="rt-toc">
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#committee">The committee's members</a></li>
    <li><a href="#powers">What the committee can and cannot do</a></li>
    <li><a href="#findings">Recommendations agencies reject</a></li>
    <li><a href="#savings">Savings estimates</a></li>
    <li><a href="#meetings">Meetings and votes</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

<section class="rt-section" id="committee">
  <h2>The committee's members</h2>
  <p>The law sets the committee's makeup ({{ law("67764", "13–14") }}). Of its {{ n_voting }} voting members on the
    current roster:</p>
  <div class="rt-seats" aria-hidden="true">
    {% for s in ["operator_board", "expert", "mtc_chair"] %}{% for m in committee.by_seat[s] %}<span class="rt-seat rt-seat-{{ s }}" title="{{ m.name }}"></span>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <ul class="rt-seat-key">
    <li><span class="rt-seat rt-seat-operator_board"></span><strong>{{ n_board }}</strong> serve on the boards of the agencies under review</li>
    <li><span class="rt-seat rt-seat-expert"></span><strong>{{ n_expert }}</strong> are independent experts appointed by MTC</li>
    <li><span class="rt-seat rt-seat-mtc_chair"></span><strong>{{ n_chair }}</strong> is MTC's chair</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="rt-meta">Two more members represent the state and do not vote. A quorum is 5 voting members.
    Roster: MTC's agenda for the May 22, 2026 meeting.</p>

  <div class="rt-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Committee members">
  <table class="rt-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Member</th><th scope="col">Seat under the law</th><th scope="col">Other public role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for m in committee.members %}
    <tr id="{{ m.id }}">
      <th scope="row">{{ m.name }}<span>{{ m.committee_role }}</span></th>
      <td>{{ ioc_seats[m.seat] }}</td>
      <td>{{ m.public_role or "Not recorded" }}
        {% if m.notes %}<p class="rt-table-note">{{ m.notes }}</p>{% endif %}
        <details class="rt-more"><summary>Sources ({{ m.sources | length }})</summary>{{ source_list(m.sources) }}</details>
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p class="rt-meta">Last verified {{ committee.last_verified | date }}.</p>
</section>

<section class="rt-section" id="powers">
  <h2>What the committee can and cannot do</h2>
  <div class="rt-two">
    <div class="rt-card rt-plain-card">
      <h3>It can</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Review the consultant's Phase 1 and Phase 2 analyses, direct revisions, and adopt the final versions. {{ law("67766(a), (c)(1)", 14) }}</li>
        <li>Specify what information each agency must give for every cost-saving measure in its implementation plan. {{ law("67766(c)(2)", 14) }}</li>
        <li>Approve each agency's draft implementation plan or recommend revisions. {{ law("67766(e)", 14) }}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="rt-card rt-plain-card">
      <h3>It cannot</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Make an agency adopt a recommendation. A board may reject one by adopting a written finding, listed <a href="#findings">below</a>. {{ law("67766(f)(3)", 15) }}</li>
        <li>Decide whether an agency complies or withhold its funds. MTC does both. {{ law("67766(h)", "15–16") }}</li>
        <li>Continue after the plans are adopted. It ends once every agency adopts a final implementation plan. {{ law("67766(g)", 15) }}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="rt-section" id="findings">
  <h2>Recommendations agencies reject</h2>
  <p>An agency's board can reject an oversight committee recommendation only by adopting a written finding that it
    would have “an unacceptable impact on transit service or safety” or conflicts with other documented local
    policies. MTC must notify the Legislature within 10 business days, and each finding expires after 12 months unless
    the board renews it with an updated assessment. {{ law("67766(f)(3)", 15) }}</p>
  {% if committee.findings %}
  <div class="rt-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Written findings">
  <table class="rt-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Agency and recommendation</th><th scope="col">Basis</th><th scope="col">Adopted</th><th scope="col">Expires</th><th scope="col">Renewed</th><th scope="col">MTC notice to Legislature</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for f in committee.findings %}
    <tr id="{{ f.id }}">
      <th scope="row">{{ f.agency }}<span>{{ f.recommendation }}</span>
        <details class="rt-more"><summary>Sources ({{ f.sources | length }})</summary>{{ source_list(f.sources) }}</details></th>
      <td>{{ finding_bases[f.basis] }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.adopted_on | date }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.expires_on | date }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.renewed_on | date if f.renewed_on else "No" }}</td>
      <td>{{ f.notice_to_legislature_on | date if f.notice_to_legislature_on else "Not found" }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <p class="rt-empty"><strong>None so far.</strong> A finding can be adopted only when an agency's board adopts its final
    implementation plan, which comes after Phase 2. Each one will be listed here with its basis, expiration, renewals,
    and MTC's notice to the Legislature.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="rt-section" id="savings">
  <h2>Savings estimates</h2>
  <dl class="rt-tiles rt-tiles-2">
    <div><dt>Recommendations with a savings estimate</dt><dd>{{ savings.n_estimated }} <small>of {{ n_total }}</small></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Estimated savings, total</dt><dd>{% if savings.total %}{{ savings.total | usd }}{% else %}None{% endif %}</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p>The Phase 1 report does not estimate savings for individual strategies, so no tracked recommendation has a
    dollar figure yet. Phase 2 must evaluate cost-saving measures with metrics such as cost per passenger mile and
    subsidy per passenger mile, reported so that “results are quantifiable and actionable.” {{ law("67762(c)(1)", 13) }}
    When Phase 2 or an agency document gives a figure for a tracked measure, it will appear on that entry and in
    this total.</p>
</section>

<section class="rt-section" id="meetings">
  <h2>Meetings and votes</h2>
  <ol class="rt-meetings">
    {% for r in committee.meetings | reverse %}
    <li id="{{ r.id }}">
      <p class="rt-ms-when">{{ r.date | date }}</p>
      <h3>{{ r.title }}</h3>
      <p>{{ r.actions or "Actions not yet recorded here." }}</p>
      <p class="rt-meta"><strong>Vote:</strong> {{ r.vote_record or "Not yet published in a source reviewed here." }}</p>
      {% if r.notes %}<p class="rt-meta">{{ r.notes }}</p>{% endif %}
      <details class="rt-more"><summary>Sources ({{ r.sources | length }})</summary>{{ source_list(r.sources) }}</details>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  <p class="rt-meta">Agendas, minutes, and video of every meeting are on <a href="https://mtc.ca.gov/meetings-events">MTC's meetings page</a>.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
